# ImStudium agent rules

Read [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) (Part 2: architecture) and [docs/STUDIUM.md](../../docs/STUDIUM.md) before changing behaviour.

- **Packages:**
  - `packages/sdk` has the client, auth, `resources/*.ts` (one per Stud.IP domain), the `content/` writers, `studium.ts`, `sync.ts`, ingest and search. No Commander.
  - `packages/cli` has `cli.ts` (core commands) and `commands/*.ts` (one `register…` per area, wired in `commands/index.ts`). No raw `fetch`; use `@imstudium/sdk`.
  - `packages/mcp` has `tools.ts` and `cli-bridge.ts` (the read-only `imstudium` door, `READ_ONLY_COMMANDS` allowlist).
- `packages/cli/src/pipeline.ts` (`runSync`) is the one sync pipeline. Add new per-course content there, not in a parallel loop.
- **Read-only by default:** resources only GET. A write goes behind `--write` and stays off the MCP allowlist. Avoid reads with side effects (`/forum-discussions/{id}/postings`, `GET /courseware-structural-elements/{id}`); see `docs/API.md`.
- Every CLI `--json` output includes `schemaVersion: "1"`. Errors use `ImstudiumError` with `code`, `message` and `hint`.
- Workspace writers are idempotent (frontmatter hash) and keep `## Student notes`. Resolve paths from `course.path`.
- Ingest is one pipeline in `packages/sdk/src/ingest/local-docs.ts` (pdf-inspector for PDF, AnyDoc for the rest, lazy-loaded). No Tesseract, poppler, LibreOffice or cloud parsing. `content.md` is not LaTeX.
- Exam dates from course text stay `confirmed: false`.
- **Tests:** vitest next to the code, with **synthetic fixtures only** (`packages/sdk/src/test/`). Never use real course content, names, messages or grades.
- Run `bun run validate` (typecheck, build, tests) before proposing a change. Update CHANGELOG.md for user-facing changes.
